-module(libsodium_crypto_core_ed25519).
-moduledoc """
Low-level arithmetic on the edwards25519 curve and on scalars modulo its
prime group order L, for building custom protocols.

Points are `bytes/0` byte compressed encodings and scalars are
`scalarbytes/0` byte little-endian integers. `is_valid_point/1` accepts
only canonical encodings of points on the main subgroup; `add/2` and
`sub/2` only reject encodings that are not on the curve, so check
untrusted input first. Scalars are used as given: there is no clamping,
unlike `m:libsodium_crypto_scalarmult_ed25519`.

`scalar_reduce/1` reduces a `nonreducedscalarbytes/0` byte value modulo
L, and `from_uniform/1` maps `uniformbytes/0` bytes (such as a hash) to a
point. Prefer `m:libsodium_crypto_core_ristretto255` for new protocols, as
it avoids the cofactor pitfalls of edwards25519.

```erlang
P = libsodium_crypto_core_ed25519:random(),
Q = libsodium_crypto_core_ed25519:random(),
1 = libsodium_crypto_core_ed25519:is_valid_point(P),
R = libsodium_crypto_core_ed25519:add(P, Q),
P = libsodium_crypto_core_ed25519:sub(R, Q),
S = libsodium_crypto_core_ed25519:scalar_random(),
One = libsodium_crypto_core_ed25519:scalar_mul(S, libsodium_crypto_core_ed25519:scalar_invert(S)),
One = <<1, 0:248>>.
```
""".
